{"availability":"available","full":"monkey0head/SplitLight","name":"SplitLight","description":"An Exploratory Toolkit for Recommender Systems Datasets and Splits","category":"Developer tools","language":"Jupyter Notebook","stars":32,"forks":3,"created":"2025-10-21T14:08:53Z","updated":"2026-03-14T17:28:04Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.19339","topics":["data-analysis","data-splitting","evaluation","recommender-systems"],"demo":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.19339","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T15:34:34.803Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T15:34:34.803Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T15:34:34.803Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T13:35:58.590Z","stars":32,"forks":3},{"at":"2026-10-09T15:34:34.803Z","stars":32,"forks":3}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["SplitLight is a lightweight framework for auditing recommender-system datasets and evaluating splitting results. Its main goal is to help you produce trustworthy data preprocessing and splits and justify split choices via transparent, data-driven diagnostics. SplitLight can be used in Jupyter/Python scripts for comprehensive analysis and offers an easy-to-use Streamlit UI for interactive exploration, health checks, and side-by-side comparisons.","SplitLight in a data-preparation pipeline. From the raw dataset to split subsets, SplitLight audits data, flags problems, and enables side-by-side comparison of alternative splits to justify the selected evaluation protocol."],"features":["Trustworthy evaluation — Poor or inconsistent train/validation/test splits lead to overoptimistic metrics and non-reproducible research. SplitLight helps you detect leakage, cold-start issues, and distribution shifts…","Transparent diagnostics — Instead of treating the split as a black box, you get concrete stats: shared interactions, temporal overlap, leaked targets, cold user/item shares, and temporal deltas between input and target.","Flexible workflow — Use the Streamlit app for ad-hoc audits, or call src/stats and src/splits from your own pipelines and notebooks (see the demo notebook)."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/monkey0head/SplitLight/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e361a761a3e2ffe728f283cd2ebb98c66be9f83ac52dfd432df2904bcf3806ba","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T13:35:58.673Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T13:35:58.673Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"SplitLight is a lightweight framework for auditing recommender-system datasets and evaluating splitting results. Its main goal is to help you produce trustworthy data preprocessing and splits and justify split choices via transparent, data-driven diagnostics. SplitLight can be used in Jupyter/Python scripts for comprehensive analysis and offers an easy-to-use Streamlit UI for interactive exploration, health checks, and side-by-side comparisons.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/monkey0head/SplitLight/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"e361a761a3e2ffe728f283cd2ebb98c66be9f83ac52dfd432df2904bcf3806ba","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/monkey0head/SplitLight/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T13:35:58.673Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-03-14T17:28:04Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/monkey0head/SplitLight/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T13:35:58.674Z","hash":"e361a761a3e2ffe728f283cd2ebb98c66be9f83ac52dfd432df2904bcf3806ba","originalBytes":12802,"storedBytes":12802,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["split","data","dataset","runs","splitlight","splits","streamlit","temporal","configs","python","stats","time","see","train","cold","core","export","notebook","preprocessed.csv","pwd","src","test","user","validation","bash","config","input.csv","item","leakage","preprocessing","pythonpath","raw","raw.csv","run","splitting","summary","target.csv","type","under","demo","demo.ipynb","distribution","example","leave-one-out","page